&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Community and Product Policy team creates and evolves principled policies that establish the rules of the road for guests and hosts across Airbnb. We solve complex marketplace and Trust &amp;amp; Safety challenges using data, stakeholder collaboration, and excellent judgement to support our community at scale. We team up with our cross-functional partners to create clear and accessible policy enforcement guides and to continuously measure, maintain, and improve our policies. We handle policy escalations and consults from across the business to ensure tough calls are resolved in accordance with our principles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a seasoned policy expert, with experience handling complex escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love solving problems and have a track record of strong cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an experienced communicator, with exceptional writing skills and presentation skills, including to senior executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are principled and rigorous — you incorporate diverse perspectives in pursuit of the best decisions and outcomes possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent with AI tools for gaining operational efficiency, but you exercise excellent judgement and know human expertise and supervision is paramount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can build and interrogate prompting, automated workflows, data queries, and stress-test model output before it reaches a decision-maker — you know when a number is not trustworthy and how to course correct&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a team player who thrives in a fast-moving environment and brings a strategic mindset to your work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Consults and Escalations Manager in Community Policy&lt;/strong&gt;, you will work across the business to understand every aspect of a case. You’ll provide timely policy analysis and corresponding enforcement recommendations, and continuously evaluate and improve our policies to handle new issues as they arise. You will resolve individual user matters and translate what you learn into policy insights and recommended changes — using your case handling expertise alongside AI and data tooling you will detect patterns across escalation volume. You&#39;ll automate things like detection and reporting, but you&#39;ll make the judgment call, document the reasoning, and own the outcome. You will help our leaders understand recurring issues and how we can fix them in the future. This role will serve as an important player in developing our global policy improvements and will have a direct impact on the peace of mind of millions of Airbnb community members around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive complicated escalations and issues towards a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise our operations teams on cases where there are policy gaps to arrive at a solution that is guided by Airbnb’s principles and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders across the business including but not limited to the Global Operations, Supply, Public Policy, Legal, Product, Trust and Safety, Communications and Partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-assisted detection of repeat policy questions and gray areas, turning consult volume into a standing signal to help drive trainings and policy clarifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Query, join, and visualize operational data to evaluate policy performance and pressure-test policy improvement recommendations before they reach leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship workflows that reduce avoidable consults, cut handling time on the rest, and measure the gain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise final judgment on ambiguous, high-exposure escalations, and make the reasoning exceptionally clear to Legal, Ops, and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience in an Operations, Policy, Legal, or Trust and Safety role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of strong leadership in handling issues and escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated capacity for critical thinking, research, and analysis; strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and presentation abilities to explain and simplify complex information to others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thoughtful business judgment, strategic thinking, and ability to work well under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a matrix and driving solutions to complex problems through cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in data analysis and demonstrated use of AI tools to create operational leverage — with the discipline to validate any output and the judgment to know what should not be delegated to a model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with operations teams, preferably in the &lt;strong&gt;Trust and Safety space&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or piloting&lt;strong&gt; AI/LLM-assisted workflows in operations, policy, or compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with quality measurement or QA frameworks for frontline teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb’s Public Policy campaign team exists to further the interests of our community of hosts and guests with politicians, regulators, opinion leaders and others who shape the political and regulatory context for our business, helping them understand the significant social and economic contributions of our platform. Across the region, we are engaged in hundreds of local conversations and negotiations with governments big and small.&amp;nbsp; We engage governments at local, state, provincial and national levels directly and also use innovative advocacy and partnership strategies that actively involve our community and stakeholders in making the case for fair, progressive home sharing rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The main role of the Public Policy Manager is to ensure the conception and execution of successful policy campaigns in their assigned region. In coordination with the Public Policy Lead, the Public Policy Manager will draft, develop and execute integrated government relations, communications, stakeholder engagement and mobilization plans and projects to achieve key policy objectives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Public Policy Manager, you must be meticulously organized, detail- and solutions-oriented. You are also able to see the big picture and prioritize projects strategically when needed, while understanding how to synthesize legislation, information and data that should be escalated to leadership. You should have a strong independent work ethic and excellent communication skills, and an ability to take big ideas and translate them into policy with a positive and creative outlook. The ability to develop and maintain good and strong relationships with key internal functions and stakeholders in the region and globally within Airbnb will be highly valued.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement Airbnb’s legislative and public policy objectives, including helping determine advocacy priorities, positions, and strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review legislative language, draft comments, and research issues to provide analysis and critical thinking on legislation affecting Airbnb’s priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain relationships with an extensive network of contacts in local, regional, and national legislative, executive, and administrative offices, as well as with allied groups and coalition partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Airbnb in meetings with government and elected officials, as well as industry associations, Airbnb hosts, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage consultants and agencies to support campaign plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure progress is reported accurately and regularly, and roadblocks are flagged in a timely fashion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional partners to make sure that policy plans fit with business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and track legislation and regulatory matters as directed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support as needed to help implement Airbnb’s legislative and public policy activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic engagement with the National Assembly, ministries, regulators, and policy stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define stakeholder strategies and engagement priorities aligned with business and policy objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive initiatives from concept through delivery, including planning, sequencing, internal alignment, and external follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise sound judgment in external communications, commitments, and escalation management in sensitive policy environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain structured engagement with local district offices, ensuring commitments are realistic, messaging is consistent, and execution is disciplined.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate political dynamics, timing risks, and stakeholder sensitivities and translate them into clear recommendations for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce concise, decision-ready briefing materials, meeting readouts, and leadership updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+years experience working with policy issues in a relevant business, political, governmental, legislative or regulatory context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the National Assembly, central government, or equivalent policy-facing role highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly get up to speed on complex technical and regulatory issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple complex projects simultaneously and navigate a complex matrix organization with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and critical thinking skills; planning, memo-writing and budgeting/basic accounting skills with proficiency in major computer applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extremely creative; takes an entrepreneurial approach to the work with a proven track record of being proactive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly results-driven and strives to find the most efficient way to do things without sacrificing a high quality of work and/or results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator with great presentation and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acute attention to detail; extremely organized and able to help keep others organized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong work ethic, and exhibits professionalism, courtesy and strong interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to exercise judgment and maintain confidentiality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible with the ability to remain poised under pressure; adapts to situations as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embraces change and challenges with a positive and solutions-oriented approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with a sense of humor and the ability to thrive in a fast moving and sometimes stressful environment; ability to resolve complex and unfamiliar problems in a timely and efficient manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for home-sharing and the mission of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership skills and experience in managing other people and developing teams will be nice to have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel regularly within the assigned region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, enabling us to attract creatively-led people and develop the best products, services, and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations:&lt;/strong&gt; We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on Recruiting Scams:&lt;/strong&gt; Scammers sometimes pose as Airbnb recruiters to get money or personal information from candidates. A few things that will always be true for Airbnb’s hiring process: our open roles are posted on Airbnb’s Career’s Page at careers.airbnb.com, and our recruiters correspond only from @&lt;a href=&quot;http://airbnb.com&quot;&gt;airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; or @&lt;a href=&quot;http://ext.airbnb.com&quot;&gt;ext.airbnb.com&lt;/a&gt; email addresses. Our recruiters will never ask for your Social Security number, bank account details, passport, or payment app information while you are interviewing.&amp;nbsp; We’ll also never ask you to pay a fee, send money, deposit or cash a check, or purchase work-related equipment (such as a company laptop) during the interview process. We encourage candidates to remain vigilant of these recruiting scams and not share sensitive information if you do not believe an individual is actually affiliated with Airbnb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
